/// Diagnostic text: "a launch that borrows '{}' must be bound to a local
/// Task, pushed into a local collection, or waited directly (...)", with
/// one example of each form. Returns an owned string.
String scoped_launch_must_be_bound(str name) {
    return @format("a launch that borrows '{}' must be bound to a local Task, pushed into a local collection, or waited directly (`Task<T> t = launch f(&{});`, `tasks.push(launch f(&{}));` or `wait launch f(&{})`)", name, name, name, name);
}

/// Diagnostic text: "{} is `{}`, not shared: declare it `shared {}` to lock
/// it". `place` is quoted source text such as "`total`", or "this value".
/// Returns an owned string.
String lock_needs_shared(str place, str type_name) {
    return @format("{} is `{}`, not shared: declare it `shared {}` to lock it", place, type_name, type_name);
}

/// Diagnostic text: "`{}` is shared between threads: read or change it
/// inside `lock {} { ... }`". Returns an owned string.
String shared_value_outside_lock(str name) {
    return @format("`{}` is shared between threads: read or change it inside `lock {} {{ ... }}`", name, name);
}

/// Diagnostic text: "`{}` holds tasks that borrow `{}`: use it only
/// through push, len, is_empty, clear and drop, or `wait` on pop, take,
/// swap_remove or get". Returns an owned string.
String task_collection_misused(str holder, str name) {
    return @format("`{}` holds tasks that borrow `{}`: use it only through push, len, is_empty, clear and drop, or `wait` on pop, take, swap_remove or get", holder, name);
}

/// Diagnostic text: "a launch pushed into a collection can only borrow
/// with `&`: its tasks may run at once, so `&mut {}` would be shared",
/// followed by `thread_share_help`. Returns an owned string.
String task_collection_mutable_borrow(str name) {
    String message = @format("a launch pushed into a collection can only borrow with `&`: its tasks may run at once, so `&mut {}` would be shared", name);
    String help = thread_share_help(name);
    message.push_str(help.to_str());
    help.drop();
    return move message;
}

/// Help appended to a borrow conflict with a launched task: " (help: to
/// change `{}` from several threads, declare it `shared` ...)", naming the
/// two ways to share the place so the user can choose. Returns an owned
/// string.
String thread_share_help(str name) {
    return @format(" (help: to change `{}` from several threads, declare it `shared` and change it inside `lock {} {{ ... }}`, or use an atomic such as `AtomicI64` for a counter; then pass `&{}` to each task)", name, name, name);
}

/// Diagnostic text: "a launch that borrows '{}' can only be pushed into a
/// local collection declared after '{}', so the collection joins its tasks
/// first; `{}` is not". Returns an owned string.
String task_collection_declared_too_early(str name, str holder) {
    return @format("a launch that borrows '{}' can only be pushed into a local collection declared after '{}', so the collection joins its tasks first; `{}` is not", name, name, holder);
}

